.TH CLIPLEDGE 1 "10 September 2026" "0.1.0"
.SH NAME
clipledge \- native encrypted clipboard history for Cinnamon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipledge
[\-\-show|\-\-toggle|\-\-hide|\-\-pause|\-\-resume|\-\-settings|\-\-status|\-\-quit|\-\-background]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores eligible X11 clipboard content in an encrypted SQLCipher database.
The key is held in the desktop Secret Service. Enter restores content without
injecting keystrokes. Native Wayland capture is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show or hide the shelf. Suitable for a Cinnamon custom keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Remain running without displaying the shelf or prompting for a key.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print non-sensitive status without opening history when not running.
.TP
.B \-\-pause, \-\-resume
Change the user capture gate; locked or unsupported states still prevent capture.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open preferences and explicit Unlock / Retry.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Exit. Clipboard survival requires another clipboard owner.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/clipledge/history.db
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clipledge/settings.json
.SH PRIVACY
Exclusion and structured-secret detection are best effort. History deletion does
not clear the live clipboard or erase external backups and filesystem snapshots.
.SH AUTHOR
Clive Bostock
